{"study_accession":"PRJNA1026987","secondary_study_accession":"SRP465795","title":"Fetal-derived activated CD83+ γδ T cells expand in preterm infants with sepsis.","description":"Here, we investigated γδ T cells in a longitudinal cohort of preterm neonates during the first year of life. Our data reveal dynamic postnatal maturation patterns of γδ T cell subsets, which are largely age-dependent. We report on the expansion of fetal-derived γδ T cells in preterm neonates with sepsis. Single cell transcriptome analyses identified HLA-DRhigh and CD83+ γδ T cells in neonatal sepsis. Overall design: Combined single-cell transcriptome (scRNA-seq) and single-cell γδTCR-seq (scTCR-seq) analysis was conducted from peripheral blood.","pubmed":"38753245","geo_series":"","n_samples":2,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN37776371","study_accession":"PRJNA1026987","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"pbmc,40,bcd#","description":"pbmc,40,bcd#","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM7837239","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":4,"first_public":"2024-05-26","attributes":[["source_name","pbmc"],["tissue","pbmc"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR26358777","experiment_accession":"SRX22066172","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"NextSeq 500","read_count":36963726,"base_count":2143896108,"first_public":"2024-05-26","experiment_title":"NextSeq 500 sequencing: GSM7837239: pbmc,40,bcd# Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"},{"run_accession":"SRR26358778","experiment_accession":"SRX22066172","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"NextSeq 500","read_count":36222654,"base_count":2100913932,"first_public":"2024-05-26","experiment_title":"NextSeq 500 sequencing: GSM7837239: pbmc,40,bcd# Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"},{"run_accession":"SRR26358779","experiment_accession":"SRX22066172","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"NextSeq 500","read_count":36753859,"base_c